From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 04 Nov 2026 08:40:00 +0000
Subject: media: cedrus: reset the VE before each MPEG-4 Part 2 job

The MPEG engine keeps some state from one MPEG-4 Part 2 picture to the
next that no register clears. Depending on the pictures decoded before,
the first coded macroblocks of a P or S(GMC) picture are then predicted
from the far right of the reference picture instead of from their own
position. The error spreads until the next I picture. In an Xvid GMC
stream this hit frame 24, and the same frames decoded correctly with a
different decode history (another stream before, a fresh process).

Neither the sprite registers, the motion vector registers, the MC cache
enable nor the reference addresses change it. The bitstream does not
matter either: rewriting the sprite trajectory of the frame, or of the
S-VOPs before it, leaves the corruption in place. A VE reset before each
job removes it everywhere: 0 bad macroblocks in four Xvid GMC/P streams,
and no change in the ISO/IEC 14496-4 results. It costs no measurable
decoding time (1080p60 Xvid, B + qpel + GMC: 6.41 s against 6.45 s for
300 frames).

Do it for H.263 and Sorenson Spark too, which run in the same engine
through the same setup.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec.c
index 266d98702..639c337ab 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec.c
@@ -24,6 +24,13 @@
 #include "cedrus_dec.h"
 #include "cedrus_hw.h"
 
+static bool cedrus_is_mpeg4_part2(u32 pixelformat)
+{
+	return pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG4_SLICE ||
+	       pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_H263_SLICE ||
+	       pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_SPK_SLICE;
+}
+
 void cedrus_device_run(void *priv)
 {
 	struct cedrus_ctx *ctx = priv;
@@ -162,11 +169,19 @@ void cedrus_device_run(void *priv)
 	 * whenever the engine is switched to or from VP9, as the vendor
 	 * library does whenever it sets up a decoder; every job programs all
 	 * the registers and SRAM it uses.
+	 *
+	 * The MPEG-4 Part 2 engine keeps state from one picture to the next
+	 * that no register clears: the first macroblocks of a P or S picture
+	 * then predict from the far right of the reference picture instead
+	 * of their own position, depending on the pictures decoded before.
+	 * Reset the VE before each of its jobs; the reset takes a few
+	 * microseconds.
 	 */
-	if (dev->last_src_pixelformat &&
-	    dev->last_src_pixelformat != ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat &&
-	    (dev->last_src_pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP9_FRAME ||
-	     ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP9_FRAME))
+	if ((dev->last_src_pixelformat &&
+	     dev->last_src_pixelformat != ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat &&
+	     (dev->last_src_pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP9_FRAME ||
+	      ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP9_FRAME)) ||
+	    cedrus_is_mpeg4_part2(ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat))
 		reset_control_reset(dev->rstc);
 	dev->last_src_pixelformat = ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat;
 
